# Test fixtures are served verbatim as HTTP responses and some assertions match
# exact bytes (e.g. b"User-agent: *\nDisallow: /"). Git's autocrlf would rewrite
# them to CRLF on Windows checkout and break those tests. Keep them byte-exact.
brand-ai-readiness-audit/tests/fixtures/** -text

# Everything else: normalise to LF in the repository.
* text=auto eol=lf
